Revision history for Imager::File::SIXEL

1.001  2026-10-04
    - The figures in Imager::File::SIXEL::Examples show on MetaCPAN
      instead of gray placeholders: the pod loads them from the
      release's tag on GitHub.

1.000  2026-10-04
    - First release.
    - Reads SIXEL images: 7-bit and 8-bit control strings, RGB and HLS
      colour definitions, raster attributes, transparent backgrounds,
      registers redefined while painting, several images per stream,
      and truncated data on request.
    - Writes SIXEL images with adaptive (histogram splitting refined by
      k-means), web-safe or caller supplied palettes, Floyd-Steinberg,
      ordered or no dithering, and transparency.
    - Encodes 640 x 480 frames in 3 to 16 milliseconds on a current
      desktop CPU, fast enough for animations at 60 frames per second,
      with output typically smaller than libsixel's for the same pixels.
